e people are smart.Dave is blue and smart, so that checks out.Doesn\'t help with being big.\n\nRule 2: If Fiona is green and blue, Fiona is big.But Fiona\'s color?The context says Fiona is blue, but it doesn\'t mention Fiona being green.So unless we can infer Fiona is green, this rule might not apply here.Since Fiona\'s greenness isn\'t stated, maybe that\'s irrelevant for Dave.\n\nRule 3: Smart people are cold.Dave is both smart and cold, so that\'s consistent.Again, not directly related to big.\n\nRule 4: If Bob is kind and blue, then Bob is not green.Wait, the context says Bob is kind?Let me check again.Wait no, looking back: the context lists Dave as kind, but Bob?Let me recheck the given facts.\n\nLooking again: The context says:.\n\nBob is blue, cold, green.\n\nDave is kind, smart, etc.Wait, the Bob\'s attributes are: blue, cold, green.Does Bob have kind?Let me check the original context again:.\n\nOriginal context:.\n\nBob is blue.Bob is cold.Bob is green.\n\nDave is blue.Dave is cold.Dave is green.Dave is kind.Dave is smart.Dave is white.\n\nErin is smart.Fiona is blue..\n\nSo Bob is not listed as kind.So the antecedent of rule 4 (Bob is kind and blue) is false because Bob isn\'t kind.So that rule doesn\'t affect anything here.So Bob\'s green status is unaffected by that rule.\n\nRule 5: If someone is blue, then they are white.Dave is blue, so he must be white.Which he is, as per the context.So that\'s okay.\n\nRule 6: Green people are white.Dave is green and white, so that\'s good.\n\nRule 7: All big people are kind.So if someone is big, then they must be kind.The contrapositive is if someone isn\'t kind, they aren\'t big.But this rule might help if we can find if Dave is big.\n\nRule 8: If someone is cold, then they are green.Dave is cold and green, so that\'s okay.Bob is also cold and green, which matches.\n\nNow, the key is to see if Dave is big.Let\'s see what could make someone big.The only rule that mentions being big is rule 2: If Fiona is green and 