tatement 5), so the cat must need the mouse (via statement 11).\n   - **Statement 17**: If the cat needs the mouse, then the mouse needs the cow.  \n     - Since the cat needs the mouse (from statement 11), this triggers statement 17, requiring the mouse to need the cow.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The mouse needs the cow due to the chain of reasoning:  \n     *Cat sees the bear \u2192 Cat needs the mouse (statement 11)* \u2192 *Mouse must need the cow (statement 17)*.  \n   - The statement \"The mouse does not need the cow\" is therefore **false** because the mouse is logically required to need the cow.\n\n**Answer**: B) False",
