s not conflict with the lion being young (fact 10) since the context doesn\u2019t state exclusivity of youth.  \n- **Conditional 19**: If the lion eats the cow, it visits the bald eagle.  \n  - The cow is eaten by the bald eagle (fact 1), so this does not imply the lion eats the cow.  \n\n### **Analysis of \"Lion is Round\":**\n- Roundness is only explicitly attributed to the cow (fact 4).  \n- **No rule or implication** in the conditionals connects roundness to other entities (e.g., the lion).  \n- There is **no contradiction** if the lion is round or not, as roundness is not tied to any other attributes (e.g., size, roughness).  \n\n### **Conclusion**:\nSince roundness is only mentioned for the cow and there is no information about the lion\u2019s shape, the statement \"The lion is round\" cannot be confirmed or denied based on the given data.  \n\n**Answer**: C) Unknown",
