 (chasing oneself) or irreflexivity (prohibiting self-chasing).\n\n3. **Inferences:**\n   - The bald eagle\u2019s actions are only stated regarding the cat. There is no information about it chasing itself.\n   - Logical systems typically assume relations can be reflexive unless explicitly restricted. Since no such restriction exists here, self-chasing is neither confirmed nor denied.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The absence of explicit information about the bald eagle chasing itself means the statement\u2019s truth value cannot be determined from the given premises. Thus, the answer is **Unknown (C)**.",
