sn't eat the bald eagle (statement 23), leading to the bald eagle being not round.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:\n   - The bald eagle cannot be round because the necessary conditions for it to be round are not met. The squirrel does not eat the bald eagle, and the rules do not provide another path to conclude the bald eagle is round.\n\nFinal Answer: \\boxed{B}",
