art, so \"If something is big and smart, then it is cold\" (statement 10) holds (she is already cold).\n   - **Contradiction**: Fiona being big and smart (via redness) forces her to be **kind** (via \"Cold + Smart \u2192 Kind\"), which contradicts her explicit non-kind status. Thus, Fiona cannot be red.\n\n**Conclusion**: Fiona cannot be red due to the contradiction it creates. Therefore, the statement \"Fiona is not red\" is **true**.\n\n**Answer**: A) True",
