 people are quiet.\n6. **Conclusion**: The premises lead to an inconsistency (Bob must be both quiet and not quiet). In such cases, logical systems cannot definitively determine the truth value of a statement due to inherent contradictions. \n\nThus, the statement \"Bob is quiet\" cannot be definitively determined as true or false due to the contradiction in the premises. \n\n**Answer: C) Unknown**",
