o she must be **cold**.\n   - **Rule 3:** \"If something is cold, it is young.\"\n     - Anne is cold and already young, so no conflict.\n   - **Rule 6:** \"All young, rough things are white.\"\n     - Anne is young and rough, so she must be white (already inferred).\n   - **Rule 8:** \"All white, young things are rough.\"\n     - Anne is white and young, so she must be rough (already given).\n\n3. **Checking for Contradictions:**\n   - None of the rules conflict with Anne being red. All derived attributes (red, green, white, cold) comply with the rules.\n   - The statement \"Anne is not red\" contradicts Rule 4, which mandates she is red.\n\n**Conclusion:** The statement \"Anne is not red\" is **false** because Anne must be red according to the given rules. \n\n**Answer:** B) False",
