ion eats lion).  \n\n2. **Condition 18**: If something eats the lion, it sees the cow.  \n   - Since the lion eats itself (from above), it must see the cow.  \n\n3. **Condition 11**: If something sees the cow and the cow eats the squirrel, then the cow is red.  \n   - The lion now sees the cow (from step 2).  \n   - The cow eats the squirrel (given).  \n   - Both conditions of the antecedent are met, so **the cow must be red**.  \n\n**Conclusion**: Since the cow is red, the statement \"The cow is not red\" is false.  \n\n**Answer**: B) False",
