not big\":\n\n1. **Given**: Anne is nice.\n2. **Rule 4**: If someone is nice, they are smart. Thus, Anne is smart.\n3. **Rule 6**: All smart people are blue. Hence, Anne is blue.\n4. **Rule 7**: Blue and smart people are furry. Since Anne is both, she must be furry.\n5. **Rule 1**: If someone is furry and nice, they are cold. Anne satisfies both, so she is cold.\n6. **Rule 9**: All cold people are big. Therefore, Anne must be big.\n\nThe conclusion is that **Anne must be big** based on the rules. The statement \"Anne is not big\" is **false** because the logical implications force her to be big.\n\n**Answer**: B) False",
