-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Anne's Attributes:**  \n   - Anne is explicitly stated to be **round**.\n\n2. **Rule Analysis:**  \n   - **Rule 1:** \"All round things are cold.\"  \n     Since Anne is round, this rule directly implies **Anne must be cold**.  \n\n3. **Additional Confirmations:**  \n   - **Rule 7:** \"Furry, round things are cold.\"  \n     Anne is both furry and round, so this rule also enforces her to be cold.  \n   - **Rule 2:** \"Cold, furry things are rough.\"  \n     Anne is cold (from Rule 1), furry, and rough, which aligns with this rule.  \n   - **Rule 6:** \"Big, cold things are furry.\"  \n     Anne is big and cold (from Rule 1), so this rule confirms her furrieness, which she has.  \n\n4. **Conclusion:**  \n   All rules consistently enforce that **Anne must be cold**. Therefore, the statement \"Anne is not cold\" is **false**.  \n\n**Answer:** B) False",
